    <briefdescription>
<para>Registry for topic handler factories. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The registry manages handler factories and creates handler instances. Teams can register custom handlers for specific topic types.</para>
<para>Built-in handlers:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>&quot;camera_data&quot;: Image scaling, JPEG compression, protobuf conversion</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>For simple topic forwarding (without custom processing), use the gateway with explicit_topics instead of creating a handler.</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Register<sp/>a<sp/>custom<sp/>handler</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">HandlerRegistry::instance().registerHandler(&quot;my_sensor&quot;,</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[](rclcpp::Node*<sp/>n,<sp/>const<sp/>HandlerConfig&amp;<sp/>c,<sp/>FoxgloveLogger*<sp/>l)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>return<sp/>std::make_unique&lt;MySensorHandler&gt;(n,<sp/>c,<sp/>l);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Create<sp/>a<sp/>handler<sp/>for<sp/>a<sp/>topic</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">auto<sp/>handler<sp/>=<sp/>registry.createHandler(&quot;my_sensor&quot;,<sp/>node,<sp/>config,<sp/>logger);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
